{"year":"2025","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 78th edition was held on February 16, 2025, at the Royal Festival Hall in London, again hosted by David Tennant. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 974576, 'screen_type': movie}\">Conclave</a> (2024) led the nominations, with 12, and ended the night with four awards, including Best Film and Outstanding British Film, the same number as <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 549509, 'screen_type': movie}\">The Brutalist</a> (2024), which won Best Director for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 55493, 'screen_type': person}\">Brady Corbet</a> and Best Leading Actor for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 3490, 'screen_type': person}\">Adrien Brody</a>. The edition debuted the Best Children's & Family Film category, won by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 929204, 'screen_type': movie}\">Wallace & Gromit: Vengeance Most Fowl</a> (2024), and had the Brazilian film <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1000837, 'screen_type': movie}\">I'm Still Here</a> (2024) among the nominees for Best Film Not in the English Language."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":974576,"name":"Conclave","image_path":"/7pMyhSbULMkCCOQCInBYU34Qmf3.jpg","director":"Edward Berger","winner":true},{"type":"movie","id":1064213,"name":"Anora","image_path":"/v8Pq2MwPXWDCg1MF3UxNlBCkgDA.jpg","director":"Sean Baker","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":549509,"name":"The Brutalist","image_path":"/52iVP3AtNtpjFiBxlOYCUPXhr47.jpg","director":"Brady Corbet","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":661539,"name":"A Complete Unknown","image_path":"/tXNPJ3XvF4RaEV66Qm9QO3pu3w7.jpg","director":"James Mangold","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":974950,"name":"Emilia Pérez","image_path":"/8ZOvbX3gCZZatUfaIZFFSAdiboW.jpg","director":"Jacques Audiard","winner":false}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Outstanding British Film","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":974576,"n